Thanks all for your feedback.

I did wonder, Steve, whether it might be one of those things that comes out in the wash with pooling robustness, but is that then mixing detection and availability probabilities at farther distances, while it's purely detection at closer distances given cameras are typically placed in a clearing of some nature? The vegetation may not act as just a screen, but actually takes up space that might prevent an animal from being in the same location within the point (at least for some species; although that can be accounted by the sampling fraction parameter I suppose).
Cheers
Darryl

